Wine @WINE_VERSION@ and MacSW's changes to Wine, Wine-Mono, 7-Zip and some of the
libraries in Contents/Resources/Wine/lib. You can get the complete source code
that corresponds to this build, and you can change it and build it again under
the terms of those licences. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt lists every part, its
licence and the licence texts. Wine is licensed under the LGPL, version 2.1 or
later; a copy is in Contents/Resources/licenses/Wine/LGPL-2.1.txt.

1. MacSW, with its Wine patches
   This build was made from MacSW source commit:
   @GIT_COMMIT@
   That source tree holds the Wine patches (patches/wine-crossover), the
   script that applies them and builds the changed Wine modules
   (scripts/build_winemac.sh), and the scripts that package this app.
   It is in MacSW-@APP_RELEASE@-source.tar.gz (see "How to get these files").
@MACSW_SOURCE_ONLINE@
@MACSW_SOURCE_TAG@

2. Wine, the upstream source archive that the patches apply to:
   @WINE_SOURCE_URL@
   SHA-256: @WINE_SOURCE_SHA256@

3. The Wine runtime that this app is based on (Gcenx build):
   @WINE_RUNTIME_URL@
   SHA-256: @WINE_RUNTIME_SHA256@
   The libraries in Contents/Resources/Wine/lib come from it unchanged. Its
   build recipes are at https://github.com/Gcenx/macOS_Wine_builds.
   The source archives of the libraries in it that are under the LGPL
   (GnuTLS, Nettle, GMP, libtasn1, libunistring, libidn2, libiconv and
   gettext's libintl), in the versions of this build:
@LGPL_SOURCES@

4. Wine-Mono: see Contents/Resources/licenses/Mono/SOURCE.txt.

5. 7-Zip @SEVEN_Z_VERSION@ (Contents/MacOS/7zz, unchanged):
   @SEVEN_Z_SOURCE_URL@
   SHA-256: @SEVEN_Z_SOURCE_SHA256@

How to get these files
Each MacSW release is published together with its source files: the source
archive of the commit in item 1 (MacSW-@APP_RELEASE@-source.tar.gz), the Wine
archive of item 2, the library archives of item 3, the Mono source archive
named in item 4 and the 7-Zip archive of item 5. For a team release, they are
also in the team's Box folder, MacSW/releases, next to the DMG. Use that copy
if you cannot open the repository in item 1. If you cannot find them, ask the
person who gave you MacSW for a copy.
